# Studio audio — no self-playback

Hearing yourself (or your keyboard) in the studio is a **feedback loop**. Built-in mic + speakers howl even with the other person in another room. Do not "fix playback" by mixing local audio into speakers.

## Invariant

Studio must **hear other people, never you** (including your second laptop / same account).

| Path | Audio |
|---|---|
| `localStream` in studio UI | **Video tracks only.** Mic lives on a private capture stream used solely by `sfu.publish`. |
| `VideoTile` / program preview | Video-only. `mixAudio: false`. Never `srcObject = getUserMedia` (muted is not enough). |
| `useRemoteAudio` | Other users' mics. Never local peer id, never same `userId`, never local audio track ids. |
| Headless recorder | `mixAudio: true` into `MediaStreamDestination` for MediaRecorder/RTMP — not speakers. |

## Banned

- Putting mic tracks on `localStream` / preview / compositor peers in the studio tab
- `createCompositor({ mixAudio: true })` in `useProgramPreview`
- `video.srcObject = stream` when `stream` still has audio tracks
- Feeding capture/getUserMedia into `useRemoteAudio`
- Connecting the compositor mix bus to `audioContext.destination` in the studio tab

## If someone reports hearing themselves / typing

The local mic is reaching that machine's speakers. Usual causes: full `MediaStream` on a media element, studio `mixAudio: true`, or another device of the same account consumed as a "remote" peer.
